- Note: `redisExec` with password uses `redisExecInput`, which sends `AUTH default <pw>\nACL LIST\n`; the fake `defaultInput` joined args is `exec -T redis redis-cli` (no "ACL LIST"), returns "OK" not ACL lines! Because `defaultInput` only checks joined args for "ACL LIST"; when using stdin, the command is in `input`, not args. The fake `defaultInput` needs to inspect `input` too. Currently:
